Enhancement: add read-only NFSv3 snapshot server

Vaultic can now expose one snapshot or subfolder with `vaultic serve nfs` for
native NFS clients on macOS, Linux, and BSD. The server uses fixed NFS and mount
protocol TCP ports, defaults to loopback, supports bounded caches and request
limits, and rejects every mutation as read-only. FUSE and NFS share the same
protocol-neutral snapshot filesystem and repository read-cache path.

Remote exposure requires explicit CIDR restrictions and acknowledgement that
NFSv3 AUTH_SYS identities are client-controlled and traffic is unencrypted.
Operator documentation includes native mount commands, VPN and SSH tunnel
guidance, readiness files, service lifecycle, and unsupported protocol features.

